{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Init.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Init.Omega"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.driver14_dt_count_not_a_qou_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.driver14_dt_count_not_a_qou_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L183-L195","doc":"**Formalize-first honest verdict (Route 1).** Neither reading of \"driver-14\nsupplies the DT count\" holds from the QOU scalar drivers: (1) no menu invariant hits\nthe count vector `(3,4)`, and (2) — the deeper obstruction — the `5₂` count is a\nchirality-split 2-set, which no single-valued scalar invariant can equal. The\nBehrend-weighted character-variety DT count is therefore **not constructible as a\nscalar QOU invariant**; it is an inherently chirality-refined geometric count of the\nspectral curve — external input, exactly as #4599's per-knot negative and the\nRossmann-CC partition-level verdict independently found. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.no_scalar_matches_chirality_split_datum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.no_scalar_matches_chirality_split_datum","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L164-L179","doc":"**The chirality-refinement obstruction (the precise missing driver-14 input).**\nNo scalar knot invariant `f : KKnot → Int` has its one-element datum `[f 5₂]` equal\n(as a set) to the `5₂` DT datum `{3,4}`: matching would force `f 5₂ = 4` and\n`f 5₂ = 3`, i.e. `4 = 3`. Hence the character-variety DT count is **not** any scalar\nEuler characteristic / recursion order / block count; supplying it requires a\n**chirality-refined, set-valued moduli count** — an object outside the scalar-integer\nrange of the 13 drivers. This is the sharpened, formalized name of the missing\n\"driver-14\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.scalar_datum_single_valued","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.scalar_datum_single_valued","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L156-L162","doc":"A **scalar** knot invariant `f : KKnot → Int` produces a single value per knot;\nits associated one-element datum `[f K]` has all members equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtDatum_fiveTwo_two_distinct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtDatum_fiveTwo_two_distinct","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L150-L154","doc":"The `5₂` DT datum has **two distinct** members (`4 ≠ 3`) — the chirality split\nof `FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.qou_scalars_miss_dt_vector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.qou_scalars_miss_dt_vector","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L139-L145","doc":"Explicit corollary form: the two genuinely QOU-derivable non-constant scalars\n(block count / Euler total are knot-independent, so cannot even *vary* with the\nknot; recursion order varies but as `(2,3)`) all miss `(3,4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.no_menu_invariant_hits_dt_vector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.no_menu_invariant_hits_dt_vector","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L131-L137","doc":"**Route-1 cross-knot exclusion.** No integer in the QOU driver menu (nor in\nthe classical control set) has value-vector `(3,4)` over `(4₁, 5₂)`: every menu\nvector differs from `dtVector`. So no single natural scalar knot-integer — Hecke\nblock count, Wedderburn Euler total, AJ recursion order, crossing, determinant,\ntetrahedra, braid index, genus — reproduces the character-variety DT count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtVector_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtVector_eq","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtVector","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtVector","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L124-L125","doc":"The DT count vector to hit: `(dtMax 4₁, dtMax 5₂) = (3,4)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.menuVectors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.menuVectors","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L113-L122","doc":"**The menu**, as the list of its `(f 4₁, f 5₂)` value-vectors. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.seifertGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.seifertGenus","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.braidIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.braidIndex","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.idealTetrahedra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.idealTetrahedra","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.determinant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.determinant","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.crossingNumber","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.crossingNumber","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L104-L107","doc":"Classical control invariants (crossing number, knot determinant `|Δ_K(−1)|`,\nminimal ideal-tetrahedron count, braid index, Seifert genus). Included to show the\nDT count is not *any* natural knot integer, QOU-derived or classical. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.recursionOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.recursionOrder","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L97-L102","doc":"QOU-owned recursion order = order of the AJ `q`-difference annihilator\n= `A`-polynomial `L`-degree = GGM Stokes-matrix dimension. `4₁ ↦ 2`\n(proved sorry-free `AJFigureEightAnnihilation`), `5₂ ↦ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.partitionEulerAbs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.partitionEulerAbs","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L93-L95","doc":"`|Σ_{λ⊢3} Δ_λ|`, the QOU Wedderburn/Springer signed-Euler total over `H₃`\n(`= |−2| = 2`, `partitionEuler₃` of #4599). Knot-independent (`2,2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.blockCountH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.blockCountH3","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L89-L91","doc":"Wedderburn block count: both `4₁` and `5₂` are 3-braids, home `H₃(q)`, whose\nblocks are the 3 partitions `λ ⊢ 3`. Knot-**independent** (`3,3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtMax","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L77-L81","doc":"The maximal DT off-diagonal count per knot (the `dtOffDiagMax` of #4599):\n`4₁ ↦ 3`, `5₂ ↦ 4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.dtDatum","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L66-L75","doc":"**The imported character-variety Behrend/BPS DT datum**, as the *set* of\nleading off-diagonal Stokes integers. `4₁` (amphichiral) carries the single\ninteger `3` (`StokesQZeroDTCount`: `S⁺(0)₀₁ = 3`). `5₂` (chiral) carries the\n**chirality-split** pair `{3,4}` — `4` in `S⁺(0)`, `3` in `S⁻(0)`\n(`FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit`, certified matrices). These are *imported* geometric\ncounts (spectral curve `A_K = 0` / rotated 3d-index of `T[K]`), recorded only to\ntest the QOU driver menu against them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.instDecidableEqKKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.instDecidableEqKKnot","kind":"instance","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.KKnot.fiveTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.KKnot.fiveTwo","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.KKnot.fourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.KKnot.fourOne","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.KKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.KKnot","kind":"inductive","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/Driver14CharacterVarietyDTMenu.lean#L56-L60","doc":"The two keystone knots: amphichiral `4₁` (muon anchor), chiral `5₂`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}